  "notes": "USAGE:\nVery common in sports reporting, video game culture, and competitive contexts. Used with する to mean \"to compete against.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {対戦|たいせん}{相手|あいて} (opponent)\n- {対戦|たいせん}する (to compete against, to play against)\n- {対戦|たいせん}{成績|せいせき} (head-to-head record)\n- {対戦|たいせん}ゲーム (competitive game, versus game)\n\nDISTINCTION FROM HOMOPHONE:\n{対戦|たいせん} (match, competition) vs. {大戦|たいせん} (great war, world war). The kanji differ: {対|たい} (versus) vs. {大|たい} (great).",
